**Authorized effects.** {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every provenance round-trips through an entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryForkInfo", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A divergent entry is imported as a flagged fork under a new id whose provenance keeps the original id (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision', 'Same id and version, different hash'; the S3.1 brief). The provenance case is the flag, so the entry file, its database row and a kit's snapshot all carry it. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` (step 24) gains a fifth case, `ForkProvenance of EntryForkInfo`, declared together with `and EntryForkInfo = { originalId : LibraryEntryId; originalVersion : VersionNumber; originalProvenance : EntryProvenance }`: the entry, version and provenance the fork was taken from, a pulled source's licence and citation included. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.1. A fork belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged` and `categoryOrigin` answers `UserCategory`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (step 63): `kindValue` answers 5 for a fork, and `catalogueIdOpt` answers `None`, because a fork ships in no catalogue. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (step 30): the provenance definition gains a fifth shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `ForkProvenance`. Its `originalId` is a GUID, its `originalVersion` a positive version, and its `originalProvenance` a `$ref` to the provenance definition itself, so a fork of a fork validates. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file has been released. Any other complete match on `EntryProvenance` that FS0025 reports answers a fork as it answers `UserProvenance`. No other case, member or schema changes. (4) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` also covers a `ForkProvenance` whose original is `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`: it is `UserManaged` and `UserCategory`. `EntryFileJsonTests`' `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` gains a material under a `ForkProvenance` of a `SourcePullProvenance`, and one under a fork of that fork. Each round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers the material.

**Acceptance.** After the fork provenance lands, `EntryProvenance` MUST declare `ForkProvenance of EntryForkInfo`, which `protection` answers as `UserManaged`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` and `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.
